  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The aqueous solution of sodium chloride is known as brine solution. On electrolysis of brine solution, the following reactions are observed.</p><p>Oxidation reaction takes place at anode and reduction reaction takes place at cathode. The reaction</p><p>Anode:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>&#8861;</mo></msup></math></p><p>Cathode:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>&#8861;</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>&#8861;</mo></msup></math></p><p>Hydrogen and oxygen are electrode products. The remaining solution contain&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;is not obtained</p></blockquote>",
